An infinite @newterm{continued fraction} is an expression of the form
@displaymath
f \,=\, {{N_1 \over D_1 + {N_2 \over D_2 + {N_3 \over D_3 + \dots}}}.}
@end displaymath
@ifinfo

@example
           N_1
f = ---------------------
               N_2
    D_1 + ---------------
                   N_3
          D_2 + ---------
                D_3 + ...
@end example

@end ifinfo
As an example, one can show that the infinite continued fraction expansion with
